                     "48x48" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png"
                  },
                  "displayName" : "Lewis Pringle",
                  "self" : "https://stroika.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A4fe560ca-b4e1-41d1-9bdf-97b1684eda32",
                  "timeZone" : "America/New_York"
               },
               "body" : {
                  "content" : [
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "Outline of IMPL strategy:",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "> Fix messageheaderstreamscanner - to allow reset back to start (seek) on start parsing message, but cache upstream data read so far. (maybe already like this)",
                              "type" : "text"
                           },
                           {
                              "type" : "hardBreak"
                           },
                           {
                              "text" : "> Then fix ReadHeaders to only assign this wrapper once (first time through starting at a point)",
                              "type" : "text"
                           },
                           {
                              "type" : "hardBreak"
                           },
                           {
                              "text" : "> Fix Readheaders to ABORT (and reset to start) the messagehaderstreamscanner if not enough data available (so non-blocking reads)",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "> Maintain list of waiting-for-data sockets, and do select (epoll) on them - looikng for new data.",
                              "type" : "text"
                           },
                           {
                              "type" : "hardBreak"
                           },
                           {
                              "text" : "Ones with new data - try the ReadHeaders on again, and when ReadHeaders works, process the command in a thread, and otherwise reset it again, and wait some more",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "Each of these ReadHeader calls can be in a task thread.",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "Then - we NEVER do blocking reads in ReadHeader - inside a threadpool task. You STILL can kill this process (hangup) by requireming body data nd having that block (thoghh I could also fix that by requiring read at head for content length). Not needed on first pass. I THINK this can be done in a few hours, but hard to test.",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     }
                  ],
                  "type" : "doc",
                  "version" : 1
               },
