      "customfield_10001" : "1_*:*_1_*:*_7424311326_*|*_3_*:*_1_*:*_2501852547_*|*_5_*:*_1_*:*_0",
      "customfield_10012" : "0|i003xj:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "WebServer ConnectionManager (and Connection) handling restructure - so while reading headers, only one thread used.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Basically, the issue is an attack - where you send one byte of http request, and hangup webserver - so one thread allocated to each thread in pool.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "But this also makes a big differnece in conneciton wtih connection keepalives. We must split the handling process as:",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : ">> one thread (or maybe one pool) which waits on all open connection sockets which are in the state of reading headers. and then for them to select on the input and read as available just until headers parsed.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : ">> THen move state of connection to body/handle, and then assign one connection thread task to that thread pool.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "and when that response is done - even if the thread still exists - top thread handling, and send back to state of read headers and that process above.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
